# Snow: Jastrem currently has the stronger structure

Jastrem's snow proposal has a particularly useful budgeting structure:

| Seasonal accumulation | Campus | Cemeteries | Combined |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Under 12" | $36,000 | $9,000 | **$45,000** |
| 12–24" | $40,000 | $10,000 | **$50,000** |
| Each additional 12" | +$8,000 | +$2,000 | **+$10,000** |

Its disclosed special/T&M rates are also fairly straightforward: plow truck with operator **$135/hour**, skid steer **$135/hour**, loader **$250/hour**, shoveling **$75/person-hour**, Snowrator **$140/hour**, and tri-axle hauling **$300/hour**.

The major thing that still needs clarification is **what deicing labor and materials are included in those seasonal amounts**. I would not sign Jastrem until that is explicit.

Jastrem also says it will make reasonable efforts to have walks ready around **7:00 AM**. That is directionally good, but "reasonable effort" should become a contractual service standard.

I recommend:

> **On Holy Family School days, designated parking, ADA routes, entrances, emergency access and primary sidewalks shall be cleared and treated for safe use by 7:00 AM unless Saint Ann provides a different opening time.**

That gives a substantial safety margin before the 7:45–8:00 AM student-arrival period.

### Bates snow

Bates' main-campus pricing is much more event-driven:

| Snow event | Bates campus |
|---|---:|
| 0–2" | $1,300 |
| 2.1–4" | $1,757.50 |
| 4.1–6" | $2,465 |
| 6.1–8" | $3,625 |
| Above 8" | +$1,143/inch |
| Road/parking deicing | $465/application |
| Walkway deicing | $720/application |

This can work well in a low-snow winter, but it creates considerably greater **budget volatility**, especially because long-duration events, ice storms, drifting, municipal replowing and other conditions can create additional charges.

For example, even a hypothetical campus season of nine moderate snow events produces about **$18,158** before ordinary deicing. One roadway plus walkway deicing treatment for each of those storms would push that hypothetical campus cost to roughly **$28,823**, before cemetery snow costs.

That doesn't make Bates expensive or inexpensive by itself; it illustrates why the Parish needs a **common modeled winter** before comparing Bates' event pricing to Jastrem's seasonal pricing.

There is also a major contractual omission in both Bates cemetery proposals: I did not find a hard commitment corresponding to Saint Ann's requirement that cemetery roads be cleared **within 36 hours after snowfall ends**.

That must be inserted expressly.

