# My selection position today

For **lawn care**, I would keep **both firms in the competition**. Jastrem is my provisional #1 because its current scope and turf program are more coherent, but I would **not pay the current $76,581.50 without first receiving a substantial credit for naturalizing the Parish-selected first half of Saint Ann Cemetery**. Bates could become #1 if it accepts the exact same natural-area map and maintains a meaningful normalized cost advantage.

For **snow**, I would put **Jastrem first** because the seasonal structure provides better cost predictability and its campus approach is closer to Saint Ann's operating requirements. I would still require clarification of deicing/material inclusions. Bates should be asked to provide a **Parish-wide seasonal cap/not-to-exceed alternative** to its per-event pricing; that could materially improve its competitive position.

Most importantly, **I would not sign either vendor's current standard contract unchanged**.

